This product bundles a snapshot of law-map's rulebook
(https://github.com/politeuma/law-map) under src/daimonion/rulebook/:
guidance sections (sections/MANIFEST.yml, sections/VOCABULARY.yml,
sections/LICENSE, and the section files the manifest lists) plus the check
specs (checks/). The exact law-map commit is recorded in
src/daimonion/rulebook/LAWMAP_SHA. law-map is Copyright 2026 politeuma
Contributors; the code and check specs are licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0, and the section prose under CC BY 4.0 (see
src/daimonion/rulebook/sections/LICENSE). Both are redistributed
unmodified. `daimonion agents-md` copies excerpts of the prose (each
section's title, the items of its summary, and its source links) into a
project's agent guide (AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md) between the daimonion:rules
markers (daimonion:ethics before the rename), and that copied text remains
rulebook content under the same CC BY 4.0 license.

The rulebook sections summarise laws, standards, and court decisions for
engineering guidance. They are not legal advice.
